  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x229B" flags="0x0">
    <title>Intake CVTC Target - Main</title>
    <description>Exact JK00A. Address 0xB43A; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Warm/main intake-cam target surface. FUN 000bda64 interpolates it by RPM/50 byte ffff11ae and Q7 normalized-BFS scheduler snapshot ffff102c, optionally applies conditional correction 0000ab5a around raw center 128, and writes ffff1c5c. FUN 000bdc66 uses it above raw coolant 131 and blends it with cold target 0000b53a between raw coolant 106 and 131 before the result enters the intake CVTC target path. The intake-cam target identity is code-proven by its placement in two-channel CVTC dispatcher 000bd170, the coolant target selector, and the consumer that compares common reference ffff2326 with both intake-cam timing channels. A 35,808-sample target-vehicle replay validates the exact warm raw lookup, normalized-BFS coordinate, byte-interpolation order, and scheduler alignment. With downstream neutralization excluded, prior-snapshot alignment is exact for 32,256 of 33,839 comparisons and within one raw for 33,122. The Cylinder Filling physical name and 0.5 degree-per-byte output conversion remain catalog candidates: the 2026-09-17 dashboard recordings keep both actual intake bytes ffff2442/ffff2443 within two counts of a target unchanged for 100 records in 95 to 100 percent of 13,202 to 43,264 samples per bank, which proves shared raw units with the target but not the degree scale of the intake edge phase. Result disposition: consumer. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
