    <title>Exhaust CVTC Target Correction - High-Detonation State</title>
    <description>Exact JK00A. Address 0xAB4A; 4 rows x 4 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Conditional subtractive correction of the warm/main exhaust-CVTC target. When ffff2466 bit 6 is set, ffff1c5d = clamp_u8(out_b33a - out_ab4a + 128); otherwise ffff1c5d = out_b33a. Raw 128 is zero correction. Code proves centered subtractive arithmetic and the exact 4x4 lookup. The correction is subtracted from the 0000b33a output in the same centered raw units before coolant selection, so it shares the exhaust-target conversion of 0.5 crank degrees per count relative to the learned rest edge, which monitor 0008f168 fixes by comparing target ffff2327 with the actual bytes ffff2324/ffff2325 of FUN 000bfc2e. The subsystem identity follows from the downstream ffff2327 binding to exhaust-target DID 0x1166 and exhaust-VTC control and DTC consumers. The homologous HR A2L uses the same 0.5 degCA per centered count for cam-timing maps. Result disposition: consumer. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via axis evidence: indexed_by].</description>
