  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4D8D" flags="0x0">
    <title>Exhaust CVTC Target - Standstill Override</title>
    <description>Exact JK00A. Address 0x8E36; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Standstill exhaust-VTC override target. While ffff246c bit 1 is set (operational enable, engine speed between ROM8[0x8e3b] and ROM8[0x8e3a], coarse vehicle speed at or below ROM8[0x8e3c], ffff244f bit 2) and latch ffff2478 bit 4 is clear, FUN 000bfe88 writes clamp_u8(ROM8[0x8e36]+128) to ffff137e at 000c01f4 in place of the coolant-selected map byte; the demand flag, both bank enables, and the duty controller then follow it. Raw 0 is no override. Stock value 40 is +20 degCA of exhaust retard. The byte is added to the 128 center in the same raw units as surface 0000b33a and target ffff2327, so it carries the code-proven 0.5 crank degrees per count of the actual bytes that monitor 0008f168 compares with the target. It is single-copy and not a Map Switching family, so a change applies to every map slot. The 2026-09-17 captures of a Map 3 image with neutral surfaces show the override as eight excursions to raw 168 starting as the engine passed 1800 RPM at rest.</description>
