  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x94A3" flags="0x0">
    <title>Requested Torque Conversion by QH0 - Primary</title>
    <description>Exact JK00A. Address 0xE98E; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence candidate. Primary QH0/torque conversion surface. Forward lookups convert RPM and a QH0 coordinate into offset-binary requested torque; FUN 00073432 interpolates a complete row at current RPM and reverses the relation to recover the QH0 coordinate from a centered signed request. All forward consumers subtract 0x8000 from the uint16 result before signed arithmetic. The stock 16x16 contents, RPM axis, and QH0 coordinate table are byte-identical to trustful family 000175c8/00018716/00018ac6. The exact duplicate pair and bidirectional code topology select the A2L primary/trustful concept; the physical units and multiplier require hardware validation. Result disposition: consumer and inverse coordinate source.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0" flags="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x14114" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedcolcount="16" mmedmajorstridebits="16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>QH0 Flow Potential [%] [cand]</units>
      <indexcount>16</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X*0.00152588">
