  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x83D2" flags="0x0">
    <title>Engine Torque Surface</title>
    <description>Exact JK00A. Address 0x10B8E; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Offset-binary Engine Torque surface. FUN 00065928 indexes rows by current rotational-speed coordinate ffff11b6 and columns by q=min(65535,trunc(u16[ffff1024]*40960/ROM16[00009534])), then writes signed result lookup-32768 to ffff18ca. FUN 000659ae adds ffff2408 to the signed map result, applies two calibrated multipliers, saturates to int16, and writes ffff18cc; FUN 000655b4 and FUN 00065b08 consume that state in two nonlinear channels. Stock ROM8[000087ee]=0 and flat-zero map 0001245a make both multipliers unity, so stock ffff18cc=sat_s16(ffff2408+ffff18ca). The column axis is copied from ROM 0002378c to a stack buffer before interpolation. Multiplying its runtime coordinate by 100/40960 gives the exact normalized ratio 100*BFS/ROM16[00009534]; stored points 0..0xf000 therefore represent 0..150 percent of the fixed BFS reference. The VQ35HR JK00D homolog uses the byte-identical function shape with map 00012922, row axis 00016f3c, column axis 00023884, and scaler 000095f6; its larger scaler and torque range provide independent family evidence. The Cylinder Filling physical name and x*0.1 Nm output scale match the HR A2L Engine Torque Map and require hardware validation; the normalized column scale itself is code-proven. Result disposition: consumer.</description>
